  annotation = {中文辅助译名：DCOS：面向消费者的中文预训练的双任务一致性优化方案},
  abstract = {The proliferation of consumer electronics, such as smart speakers, in-vehicle systems, and smart homes, poses stringent demands for efficient and robust Chinese natural language understanding (NLU) on devices. However, prevailing Chinese language models, which largely adopt word-level strategies from English pre-training, struggle with colloquialisms, ambiguity, and new vocabulary. A key underlying issue is their neglect of the inherent exposure imbalance of Chinese characters, leading to uneven performance across downstream tasks. To address these challenges, we propose a Dual-task Consistency Optimization Scheme (DCOS) that integrates both word-level and structure-level representation learning. Inspired by the compositional nature of Chinese characters—built from components, strokes, and composite structures—DCOS combines a Masked Language Modeling (MLM) task with a novel Chinese Structure Recombination (CSR) task. While MLM learns word-level semantics via a one-to-one masking strategy, CSR explores structure-level semantics by deconstructing and reconstructing characters and their structural units. This dual-task approach enables DCOS to capture fine-grained Chinese representations and mitigates the limitations of imbalanced word-level pre-training through balanced structure-level learning. Implemented on the BERT architecture, our model achieves overall performance improvements on multiple Chinese NLP tasks, with average performance reaching state-of-the-art on reading co},
}

